0. DEFINITIONS

  "the Software" means all source code, configuration files, textures,
  documentation and build artifacts (.jar and the like) in this repository that
  were authored by the copyright holder. The third-party components listed in
  Section 4 are not part of the Software.

  "You" means any individual or entity that obtains the Software or any part of
  it by any means.

1. RESERVATION OF RIGHTS

  All rights in the Software are reserved by the copyright holder. This license
  grants no rights except those expressly stated in Section 3. Anything not
  expressly permitted is prohibited.

2. PROHIBITED ACTS

  Without the prior written permission of the copyright holder, You may not:

  1. Modify — modify, adapt, translate or create derivative works of the
     Software or any part of it;

  2. Distribute — copy, distribute, transmit, publish, lend, sell, sublicense
     or otherwise make the Software or any part of it available to any third
     party, including through modpacks, server packs, repositories or file
     sharing;

  3. View or reverse engineer — view, copy or publish the Software's source
     code, or decompile, disassemble or reverse engineer any build artifact, or
     attempt to derive source code or design from it;

  4. Cause or assist any third party to do any of the above.

3. WHAT PLAYERS MAY DO

  Solely in order to play on a server operated or expressly authorized by the
  copyright holder, You may download build artifacts distributed by the
  copyright holder and run them on Your own device. This permission is
  non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable, revocable at any time
  without cause, and covers nothing beyond running the Software — the
  prohibitions in Section 2 continue to apply.

  This section exists because the mod includes client-side screens, so a player
  who has not installed it cannot play at all. It grants the minimum needed for
  that and nothing more.

4. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

  The Software depends on, and its build artifacts may bundle, the following
  third-party works. They are not part of the Software and remain subject to
  their own licenses. Nothing in this license restricts any right those
  licenses grant You.

  - Cobblemon — Mozilla Public License 2.0
  - Fabric Loader, Fabric API, Fabric Language Kotlin — Apache License 2.0
  - kotlinx.serialization (bundled in build artifacts) — Apache License 2.0
  - Kotlin standard library — Apache License 2.0
  - Minecraft — Mojang/Microsoft End User License Agreement

  Cobblemon's MPL 2.0 is file-level copyleft. The Software does not modify
  Cobblemon's files and only calls its public API, so MPL does not reach the
  files authored by the copyright holder. Anyone who redistributes Cobblemon's
  own artifacts alongside the Software takes on MPL 2.0 Section 3's source
  availability obligations for those artifacts.

5. STATUTORY CARVE-OUT

  The prohibition on reverse engineering in Section 2.3 does not apply to the
  extent that applicable law grants a non-waivable right to do so — for example
  decompilation for interoperability under Article 101-4 of the Korean
  Copyright Act, or Article 6 of EU Directive 2009/24/EC. This license does not
  attempt to override such provisions.

6. TERMINATION

  The permission in Section 3 terminates automatically upon any breach of this
  license, and You must delete all copies in Your possession. This does not
  limit any other remedy available to the copyright holder.

7. NO WARRANTY; LIMITATION OF LIABILITY

  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. THE COPYRIGHT HOLDER
  SHALL NOT BE LIABLE FOR ANY DAMAGES ARISING FROM THE USE OF OR INABILITY TO
  USE THE SOFTWARE, to the extent permitted by applicable law.

8. CONTACT

  Permission for anything in Section 2 — modification, distribution, source
  access — must be requested from and granted in writing by the copyright
  holder (GitHub: @Duskafka).

